Implemented P5.2 record-linked channels at Tier 0/1; reports and progress log written.

**What shipped**
- Native `DISCUSSIONS` page-layout widget type (shared enum/config → front renderer/mapping → server DTO/validators → 2-39 `page_layoutWidget_type_enum` migration), auto-hidden via `discussions` relation.
- a2e-chat owns the relation pair: `chatChannel.project`/`project.discussions` (→ A2E Projects) and `chatChannel.company`/`company.discussions` (→ standard company). Install order: **Projects before Chat** (recorded per D-P4.3-DOC consumer-owns rule).
- Tabs: project layout (a2e-projects) + additive standalone tab on the standard company layout (a2e-chat `definePageLayoutTab`).
- Per-record provisioning (PROJECT kind for project, CUSTOM for company) via `useRecordChatChannels` + pure `recordChatChannel` util.
- Side-panel mini-chat (`SidePanelPages.ChatChannel`) reuses the extracted `ChatChannelConversation` — one composer/live/read surface shared with `ChatPage` (no duplicate).

**Checks (all green)**: front tsgo exit 0; server tsgo exit 0; front jest 109 + 10; server page-layout jest 86; a2e-chat typecheck/29 tests/build; a2e-projects typecheck/174 tests/build; `nx build twenty-shared` and `twenty-sdk`; oxlint --type-aware + oxfmt clean on touched files.

**Missing for tick (Tier 2 only)**: install Projects→Chat on a scratch workspace to confirm the cross-app relation resolves and the migration runner accepts a chat-owned tab on the standard company layout; browser proof of tab → provisioning → mini-chat.

Report: `docs/plan/phases/phase-05-report.md` (2026-09-18 23:20 UTC entry). Progress: `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

